  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP Resilience Sudan</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">WFP Resiliens Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The World Food Programme (WFP) har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering fr&#xe5;n Sida om 165 MSEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra det tre&#xe5;riga projektet &quot;Safety Net Activities&quot; i Sudan under perioden 2019-2022. Sida har beslutat att st&#xf6;dja de tv&#xe5; f&#xf6;rsta &#xe5;ren med 133 miljoner SEK. Ett eventuellt st&#xf6;d till ett tredje &#xe5;r &#xe4;r avh&#xe4;ngigt utfallet av den utv&#xe4;rdering som ska genof&#xf6;ras under projektets andra &#xe5;r.

Insatsen syftar till att 1) Erbjuda inkomstgenererande aktiviteter och tekniskt st&#xf6;d inom ramen f&#xf6;r sociala trygghetssystem f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja hush&#xe5;ll med bristande livsmedelsf&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning att reducera cykliska risker och hantera konsekvenser av klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar 2) Ge kapacitetsutvecklande st&#xf6;d till  jordbrukare och institutioner p&#xe5; lokal, delstats- och nationell niv&#xe5; 3) Tillhandah&#xe5;lla flygf&#xf6;rbindelser till akt&#xf6;rer inom humanit&#xe4;rt och l&#xe5;ngsiktigt utvecklingssamarbete. 

Insatsen bidrar till WFP:s strategiska plan f&#xf6;r Sudan 2019-2023. F&#xf6;rutom bidraget till WFP avs&#xe4;tts 200 000 SEK f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt uppf&#xf6;ljning samt metodutveckling.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Food Programme (WFP) has applied to Sida for funding of 165 MSEK to carry out the three year project &quot;Safety Net Activities&quot; in Sudan during the period 2019-2022. Sida has decided to fund the first two years of the project with 133 milion SEK. Possible support to a third year will depend on the outcome to the evaluation to be carried out during the second year of the project.

The intervention aims at 1) Offering asset-creation activities and technical assistance through safety nets to help food-insecure households to reduce risk and adapt to cliamte change 2) Provide capacity-strengthening support for farmers and local, state and national agricultural institutions 3) Air services are provided for the humanitarian and development community.  

The intervention has a budget of 165 MSEK and is contributing to WFP&apos;s Country Stategic Plan 2019-2023. In addition to the contribution to WFP, 200 000 SEK is set aside for increased monitoring as well as methods development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention would mainly contribute to fulfilling Strategic Outcome no 3 (SO3) of WFP&apos;s Country Strategic Plan: food insecure people in targeted areas and food systems have increased resilience to shocks by 2024. 

This would be achieved by the following broad activities, which each included a number of different outputs:

- Offer asset creation activities and technical assistance through safety nets to help food insecure households to reduce risk and adapt to climate change.

- Provide capacity strengthening support to farmers and local, state and national agricultural institutions.

- Improved access to logistics and transports for humanitarian and development actors to travel across Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
